      "finding": "Two broad fronts lead into a third whose facing remains substantial at this shoulder angle. A thick outboard S continues below its real return before bending into a C, so the required smaller third turn and short terminal C do not read as distinct sized stages. The main ribbon also has broad soft sage casts, especially in turns two and three, beyond the fine muted mint edging. The actual open spaces and existing opaque gray returns are readable and can be retained.",
