      "area": "Root under the bob and cap base",
      "finding": "Two beads are recognizable at the correct low anatomical LEFT attachment. A small opaque red sliver continues under the neighboring gray lock at about (608,305), separate in projection from the visible round bead faces. Keep the two-bead silhouette clear in any root cleanup without moving the attachment. The cap has two dominant V leaves and a short attached base flap."
    }
  ],
  "observations": [
